Track 3: Overbiased Flutter of the Swarm
- Story & Context: Decades after the legendary wedding fire, the abandoned salt flats of Trieste are said to be haunted by a metallic buzzing that mimics the manic Juno-60 chords of that fated night. Old-timers swear they can still smell burnt sugar and hot rubber rising from the cracked earth whenever the wind kicks up. Legend says the rival dynasties never actually stopped dancing, having metamorphosed into a single, migratory swarm of brass-blowing, wire-walking spirits who feed on pure adrenaline. Their spectral anthem still echoes through the ravines, warning travelers with a triumphant, distorted chant: "We traded our skins for wings, and now we never have to land!"
